# Approval design pointer

When your work touches who may decide or act, read `.cursor/skills/agentic-approval-design/SKILL.md`
and the canonical map `project-context/1.define/approval-map.md` (a draft until the operator approves it).

- **@product-mgr** (PRD, system description, stories): check new or changed requirements against the
  map. Propose requirement changes; do not apply them without operator approval.
- **@system.arch** (SAD, SFS): say where each Alone / Ask / Never row is enforced in code, and resolve
  the map's open decisions marked "SAD".
- **@backend.eng, @frontend.eng, @integration.eng, @qa.eng, @security.eng**: enforce the map on the
  server, not only in the UI, and test the map's test matrix.

Keep one map. Update it rather than creating another. The map and this rule are guidance, not enforcement.
